@host = http://localhost:8080

### Login with default Spring Security
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=marketing&password=marketing

### Test Logout
GET {{host}}/logout

### Test GET status configuration
GET {{host}}/v1/api/auth/status

### Test GET CSRF token
GET {{host}}/v1/api/auth/csrf-token

### Test GET users
GET {{host}}/v1/api/users

### Test Add User
POST {{host}}/v1/api/addUser
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Test Auth Register
POST {{host}}/v1/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "mySecurePassword"
}

### =============================================
### Facebook Config Endpoints
### =============================================

### 1. Check Facebook Token Status
GET {{host}}/v1/api/marketing/config/facebook/token/status

### 2. Update/Save Facebook Token (replace YOUR_TOKEN and YOUR_PAGE_ID)
PUT {{host}}/v1/api/marketing/config/facebook/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accessToken": "YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE",
  "pageId": "YOUR_PAGE_ID_HERE",
  "exchangeForLongLived": true
}

### 3. Refresh Token (if expired)
POST {{host}}/v1/api/marketing/config/facebook/token/refresh

### 4. Get Connected Facebook Page Info
GET {{host}}/v1/api/marketing/facebook/pages
